// Payment Orchestration (BC-6) internal interface.
//
// `payment-api` speaks this to `payment-orchestrator`. They are separate binaries so a
// slow gateway cannot consume the ingress connection pool, and so ingress scales on
// connection count while orchestration scales on in-flight gateway calls.
//
// THE TIMEOUT RULE governs this whole file. If a gateway call times out or returns an
// ambiguous transport error, the attempt is recorded TIMEOUT_UNKNOWN and the payment
// STAYS in PROCESSING. The caller receives a normal response carrying that state, not
// an error. No timer may fail a payment. Only a gateway webhook, a reconciler lookup
// keyed on our deterministic gateway idempotency key, or a settlement report can move
// it out.

